#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:119
msgid "What this theme does"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:120
msgid "A designer hands over a ZIP file. This theme turns it into a working website — the pages, the menu, the header and footer, the pictures — usually within the hour, looking the way the designer drew it. Nothing about it is a mock-up: every page is real, editable, and yours."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:122
msgid "Why it matters to the company"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:124
msgid "Speed: a delivered design becomes a reviewable site the same day, not after weeks of hand work."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:125
msgid "Faithfulness you can check: after every build the theme measures each page against the design and says what share of the design’s content it renders. A weak page is flagged, not discovered by a client."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:126
msgid "Anyone can edit: texts on the pages, the words in the header and footer, the menu — all through normal WordPress screens. No developer needed for day-to-day changes."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:127
msgid "No lock-in: it runs on any ordinary hosting. One plugin is required (ACF); WooCommerce is added only when the design turns out to have a shop in it, and the theme’s own shop templates come with it in the same step. Contact forms need no plugin at all."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:128
msgid "Reversible: one button removes everything an import created and touches nothing else."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:129
msgid "It learns: every import is written into a journal — what the archive was, what went wrong, how faithful the result measured — and the next import starts from that knowledge."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:134
msgid "How an import goes, in four steps"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:137
msgid "Upload the design ZIP on Appearance → Design import. A design already uploaded appears as a card — click it to continue with it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:139
msgid "The upload form with an already-uploaded design below it"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:140
msgid "Step 1 — the upload form, with designs already on the server listed under it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:144
msgid "Choose. The screen lists every page the build will make, the language, and — when the archive carries more than one site — a box per site. Untick what you do not want; nothing here is one-way."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:146
msgid "The build panel: conversion mode, language picker, the archive’s sites, and the list of pages the build will make"
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:147
msgid "Step 2 — mode, language, which of the archive’s sites, and exactly which pages."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:150
msgid "Build. It runs on the server; the tab can be closed. The screen narrates every step, shows a progress bar, and flags anything worth checking."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:152
msgid "Review and publish. The pages arrive as drafts with View and Edit beside each; publishing sets the front page and the menu for you. The list below the table says what the build measured and what deserves a look."
msgstr ""

