#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:161
msgid "A design that ships in several languages (en, ru, zh…) is imported one language at a time — or all at once. To add a language later: open Design import, click the design, set Language to the one you want (or to “All”), and press Build again. The new pages are created beside the existing ones, and the language switcher in the header connects to them by itself. The pages already built are left exactly as they are."
msgstr ""

#: inc/Modules/Handbook.php:162
msgid "Translating what YOU wrote (an edited heading, a new paragraph) is ordinary page editing: open the page in the other language and change its text. The theme’s own admin screens are translation-ready too — a translation file per language under languages/ is all they need."
